        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 25 at 2:47AM EDT by NWS Wilmington OH</headline>
        <description>The combination of clear skies and nearly calm winds this morning
has led to areas of fog developing, particularly along the river
valleys. However, some transient overland fog has developed, which
may be locally dense in spots. Fog is expected to burn off shortly
after daybreak.

Motorists should be prepared for rapid changes in visibility.
Allow for greater distances between vehicles, use low beam
headlights, and allow extra time to reach your destination.
</description>
